    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0010-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "1"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000087",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "contents",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0010-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "Problem Statement"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000088",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "contents",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0011-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "Our goal is to construct a data-based model which analyzes musical in\ufb02uence in terms of genre and content"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000089",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "contents",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0011-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "over the past 90 years. First, we determine a way to quantify the in\ufb02uence of individual artists based only"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000090",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "contents",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0011-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "on the influence data \ufb01le. Next, we use full music data \ufb01le to develop a metric of musical similarity. We"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000091",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "contents",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0011-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "apply this measure to analyze how genres are distinguished, how they relate to one another, and how they"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000092",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "contents",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0011-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "change over time. Then, we analyze in\ufb02uencer-follower relationships with our musical similarity metric,"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000093",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "contents",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0011-l0005"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "pinpointing the musical characteristics most correlated with in\ufb02uence. At this point, we will use all our"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000094",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "contents",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0011-l0006"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "quantitative tools to identify both moments of musical revolution as well as musical revolutionaries. We"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000095",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "contents",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0011-l0007"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "will then turn our focus to a speci\ufb01c genre, applying our tools to provide insight into the musical evolution"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000096",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "contents",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0011-l0008"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "of this category. Finally, we will compare the revolutions we identi\ufb01ed to a historical timeline of social and"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000097",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "contents",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0011-l0009"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "political developments in musical evolution."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000098",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "furniture",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0002-n0001-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      2
    ],
    "text": "\u5fae\u4fe1\u53f7\uff1aMATHmodels"
